        "title": "test: stabilize maintainer prepare baseline",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nStabilizes the local maintainer prepare baseline failures seen while preparing #85791.\n\n- updates the node-host allow-always coverage test to use a supported direct executable fixture instead of a shell-wrapped interpreter command that is rejected by the safety boundary\n- skips the chmod cleanup retry assertion under root, where root can remove through the permission-denied fixture\n- isolates mac packaging PATH fixtures from host `/usr/bin/pnpm` / `/usr/bin/corepack`\n- makes Telegram channel-post album timer tests deterministic and fail loudly on timeout\n\n## Maintainer alert\n\nThis is test-only stabilization. It does not add or change config schema/options, plugin API/contract, CLI flags, env vars, migrations, public behavior, or channel timeout behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\nOriginal full validation from WSL root at `cbf66c346b`:\n\n- targeted failing test files -> passed, 5 Vitest shards\n- five previously failed prepare shard configs -> passed individually\n- formatting and lint -> passed\n- `pnpm build` -> passed\n- `pnpm check` -> passed\n- `pnpm test` -> passed, 88 Vitest shards\n\nCurrent-head recheck at `6c770202967` on 2026-07-13:\n\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/package-mac-app.test.ts --reporter=dot` -> passed, 7 tests passed and 2 skipped\n- source inspection confirms the isolated fake `corepack` fixture uses `#!/bin/bash` with `PATH` restricted to the fixture directory; the separate fixture using `#!/usr/bin/env bash` includes `/usr/bin:/bin` in `PATH`\n- `git diff --check` -> passed\n\nNo merge performed.\n",
